      "timestamp_raw": "Sept 2, 2012 9:28:02 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Here's a clone of S. jonesii that originally came from Phil Sheridan.  This is the more \"typical\" looking jonesii that you see in cultivation these days, and a neat aspect of this particular individual is that it colors up nicely in the fall.  The plant is rather vigorous, and regularly produces offshoots:<br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/IMG_8952.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/IMG_8953.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/IMG_8951.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/IMG_8954.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/IMG_8949.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
